      "page_title": "Costs, Leaks & Shared State",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Choosing And Typing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Class-based when you need named per-function state",
            "Add `__get__` if that class decorates methods",
            "Use `ParamSpec` so typed callers keep their signatures"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Costs You Pay"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cost",
            "Where it bites"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "extra frame",
              "every call"
            ],
            [
              "`*args` packing",
              "tight numeric loops"
            ],
            [
              "`maxsize=None`",
              "unbounded memory"
            ],
            [
              "wrapper frames",
              "noisier tracebacks"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Leaks & Shared State",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@lru_cache` on a method keeps `self` alive forever",
            "State in the ==factory scope== is shared across functions",
            "Reusing one stateful decorator object bleeds state",
            "Forgetting `return wrapper` makes `f` **None**"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Caching Methods",
          "text": "Prefer `cached_property` or a per-instance dict over `@lru_cache` on methods — the cache key holds strong references."
        }
      ]
    },
