    {
      "page_title": "The Two Canonical Examples",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. The Closure Everyone Learns",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def make_adder(n):",
            "    def add(x):",
            "        return x + n",
            "    return add",
            "",
            "add5 = make_adder(5)",
            "print(add5(3))  # 8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`make_adder` is a factory, not an adder",
            "Each call builds a fresh `add` function",
            "`n` outlives `make_adder` inside a cell",
            "`add5(3) == 8` because `n` is still 5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Inspect That Cell"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Expression",
            "Value"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`add5.__name__`",
              "`'add'`"
            ],
            [
              "`add5.__code__.co_freevars`",
              "`('n',)`"
            ],
            [
              "`add5.__closure__[0].cell_contents`",
              "`5`"
            ],
            [
              "`make_adder(9)(3)`",
              "`12`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two adders never share one cell",
            "`make_adder(2) is not make_adder(2)`",
            "Same shape powers every decorator factory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Factory: Three Nested Layers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def repeat(n):",
            "    def deco(fn):",
            "        @wraps(fn)",
            "        def w(*a, **kw):",
            "            for _ in range(n):",
            "                r = fn(*a, **kw)",
            "            return r",
            "        return w",
            "    return deco"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Layer",
            "Takes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`repeat`",
              "config `n`"
            ],
            [
              "`deco`",
              "the function"
            ],
            [
              "`w`",
              "call args"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Reading The Layers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`n` is captured once, at decoration time",
            "`w` closes over both `fn` and `n`",
            "`r` holds the last call's return value",
            "`@wraps(fn)` keeps name, doc, `__wrapped__`",
            "Usage is `@repeat(3)`, parens included"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@repeat(3)",
            "def ping():",
            "    print('pong')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "One Rule, Two Shapes",
          "text": "A plain decorator takes a function and returns a replacement. A decorator factory takes configuration and returns that plain decorator. Nothing else changes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Missing-Parens Bug & Its Guards",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. The Missing-Parens Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@repeat  # wrong: no parens",
            "def ping():",
            "    print('pong')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`@repeat` passes the *function* as `n`",
            "`repeat(ping)` returns `deco`, not a wrapper",
            "`ping` is now bound to `deco` itself",
            "Decoration succeeds; nothing raises yet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "12. Why The Error Travels"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Stage",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "import time",
              "silent, no error"
            ],
            [
              "`ping()`",
              "wants a function arg"
            ],
            [
              "message",
              "`missing 1 required`"
            ],
            [
              "blame lands on",
              "the call site"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cause is the decorator line, not the call",
            "`range(n)` never runs, so `n` looks innocent",
            "Check `ping.__name__` — it reads `'deco'`",
            "Fix: write `@repeat(3)`, with parens"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "13. Guard The Factory"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def repeat(n):",
            "    if callable(n):",
            "        raise TypeError('use @repeat(k)')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Validate at ==factory time==, not on first call",
            "Reject `n < 1` with `ValueError` immediately",
            "The traceback then points at the decorator line"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "14. Support Both Shapes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "def deco(fn=None, *, x=1):",
            "    if fn is None:  # @deco(x=2)",
            "        return partial(deco, x=x)",
            "    @wraps(fn)  # bare @deco",
            "    def w(*a, **kw): ...",
            "    return w"
          ],
          "note": "x must be keyword-only"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "`fn` is"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@deco`",
              "the function"
            ],
            [
              "`@deco()`",
              "`None` → partial"
            ],
            [
              "`@deco(x=2)`",
              "`None` → partial"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`*` makes `x` ==keyword-only==, so `@deco(3)` can't slip in",
            "`partial` returns a decorator still waiting for `fn`",
            "One name, both call styles, no guessing"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
