          "a_bullets": [
            "Yes, since Python 3.8 — default `maxsize=128`",
            "It is a bare-or-called factory by design",
            "`@lru_cache()` behaves the same"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Tells you"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`f.__name__`",
              "wrapped correctly?"
            ],
            [
              "`f.__wrapped__`",
              "one layer down"
            ],
            [
              "`inspect.unwrap(f)`",
              "the original"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Factory args validated at decoration time",
            "`@wraps` on the innermost wrapper",
            "Keyword-only config keeps calls unambiguous"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Habit Worth Keeping",
          "text": "If a decorator takes any configuration, it is a factory and needs parens. A wrong bare `@repeat` fails far from its cause, so check the decorator line first."
        }
      ]
